    "time_horizon": "this-parliament",
    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "This policy broadly maintains the existing tax baseline \u2014 the corporation tax cap locks in current rates, full expensing was already in place, and the business rates reform is designed to be revenue-neutral. The main fiscal concern is that locking in these commitments reduces the government's room to raise revenue if needed, but the policy itself does not add materially to the debt path.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the business rates reform is genuinely revenue-neutral in practice, and whether full expensing's long-run GDP uplift is large enough to offset its near-term revenue cost.",
